of Fox Corporation.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Anthony J. Wood | Founder, President & CEO | Age 59 | Compensation: $1.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $1.3M ranks in the top quartile among Communication Services peers, with revenue growing 32%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $133K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $98K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Roku, Inc. is a large-cap communication services business with a $23.9B market cap on $4.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +15% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -69% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 44%.","The business throws off $478M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 5.47\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin -3.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.6%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 405% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation 